@page "/about"
<PageTitle>About our data — Dwellio</PageTitle>
<div class="shell section narrow"><span class="eyebrow">TRANSPARENCY</span><h1>Behind your matches</h1><h2>A student project for Astana</h2><p>Dwellio compares homes by cost, neighbourhood and commute. This is a local educational application. Seeded complexes and listings are fictional, coordinates are illustrative, and images are original concept illustrations. User-created listings are labelled separately.</p><h2>Transport scenarios</h2><p>Journey times and bus loads are simulated. They change by selected hour and direction, but are not live forecasts or timetables. We do not have a verified source of bus occupancy. Boarding near the start of a route does not guarantee a seat.</p><h2>Why this home?</h2><p>Mandatory requirements are checked first. Eligible homes are ranked by rent headroom, the share of your desired amenities nearby, and commute time. Each part is multiplied by your chosen weight. The 0–100 score is a comparison aid, not a probability of satisfaction.</p><h2>Missing information</h2><p>Unknown utilities are excluded from the known cost subtotal and clearly labelled. When route data is unavailable, the transport score is zero and a warning is shown. Missing information never becomes an invented positive rating.</p><h2>Privacy and limitations</h2><p>ASP.NET Core Identity hashes passwords. Saved homes and preferences belong to your account. Reviews are public; residency is not verified. This classroom version does not confirm email addresses and is not intended for real rental transactions. OpenStreetMap loads externally; listings remain usable without it.</p><h2>Technology</h2><p>C# / .NET 10, Blazor, Entity Framework Core and SQLite. Pure functions, immutable records and LINQ power the recommendation engine. The interface, calculations and persistence are separate.</p><a class="button" href="/preferences">Find my fit ↗</a></div>
